 "old_string": "A one-cell-per-tile output suggests a tile summary, not necessarily marker presence. Distinguish exact count (here exactly two) from any-marker, majority, component count, and positional-pattern hypotheses by checking every tile in each demo. Tile dimensions can change between demonstrations.\n",
 "new_string": "A one-cell-per-tile output suggests a tile summary, not necessarily marker presence. Distinguish exact count (here exactly two) from any-marker, majority, component count, and positional-pattern hypotheses by checking every tile in each demo. Tile dimensions can change between demonstrations.\n\n### Additional accepted variant: task-3174de58 (8x19, 2026-11-02)\nThe accepted test had full separator rows at 0-based rows 2 and 5 (color 2), and full separator columns at 3, 7, 11, and 15 (color 2). These delimit a 3x5 array of tiles, each 2x3. Marker color was 3 and ordinary tile/background color was 7. Per-tile marker counts were `[[1,1,1,1,2],[1,2,1,1,1],[1,1,2,1,1]]`. The accepted output was `[[7,7,7,7,1],[7,1,7,7,7],[7,7,1,7,7]]`: exactly two marker cells map to 1; all other counts map to 7. This is further evidence that separator color can be distinct from both marker and tile background, and tiles may be 2x3; exclude the separator rows/columns before counting."
